    "ls|LS17_S12_U_171": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK\n \nSABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. \n171\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON \n01\nST\n \nAUGUST\n \n2023\n \n \nFA\nR\nMERS COVERED UNDER PM\n-\nKISAN\n \n \n*\n171\n.\n \nSHRI BALASHOWRY \nVALLABHANENI\n:\n \n \nWill the Minister of \nAGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a)\n \n     \nthe details of farmer beneficiaries covered under Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman \nNidhi (PM\n-\nKISAN) since its \nimplementation, year and State\n-\nwise;\n \n \n(b)\n \n     \nwhether it is true that the number of farmers\n \nbenefited under PM\n-\nKISAN has \ncome down from55.68 lakhs in 2019 to about 30 lakhs now;\n \n \n(c)\n \n     \nif so, the reasons for such sharp decline in\n \nextending benefit to \nfarmers under \nPM\n-\nKISAN;\n \n \n(d)\n \n    \nthe efforts being made by the Government to\n \ncover more and more farmers under \nPM\n-\nKISAN\n \nparticularly from Andhra Pradesh?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n      \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n               \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR)\n \n \n      \n(a) to (d)\n:\n \n    \n \nA Statement is laid on the table of the House.\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \nSTATEMENT MADE IN REPLY TO \nLOK\n \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. \n171\n \nRAISED BY SHRI \nBALASHOWRY VALLABHANENI\n, DUE FOR REPLY ON \n01\n-\n0\n8\n-\n2023\n.\n \n \n(a)\n:\n \nThe Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman Nidhi (PM\n-\nKISAN), a Central Sector Scheme, \naims at providing financial assistance to cultivable landholding farmer families across the \ncountry, subject to certain exclusion criteria. Unde\nr the Scheme, an amount of Rs. 6000/\n-\n \nis transferred annually in three equal \ninstalment\ns of Rs.2000/\n-\n \ndirectly into the Aadhaar \nSeeded bank accounts of the farmers. \n \nSo far, more than 2.60 lakh Cr have been disbursed \nto over more than 11 Cr farmers families. \n \n \n \n \nThe details of beneficiary farmers under the PM\n-\nKISAN Samman Nidhi (PM\n-\nKISAN\n), period wise \n \nand State\n-\nwise, \nsince\n \ninception\n \nof the scheme \n \nis enclosed in \nAnne\nxure I.\n \n \n(b) & (c)\n:      \n \nDoes not arise.\n \n \n(d)\n:\n \n \nIn Andhra Pradesh, the number of beneficiaries has increased from 33.16 lakhs in \nthe 1\nst\n \ninstalment period (December 2018 \n–\n \nMarch 2019) to 41.33 lakhs in the 14\nth\n \ninstalment period (April 2023 \n–\n \nJuly 2023).\nUnder the PM\n-\nKISAN Scheme, the responsibility \nto identify the beneficiaries and upload their correct and verified data on PM\n-\nKISAN portal \nlies with the respective State/UT Government. Thereafter, these data go through various \nlevels of verification and validation including Aadhaar/PFMS/Income Tax database. \nSubsequent to such verification and validation, the benefit of the Scheme is passed on\n \nto \neligible beneficiaries directly into their Aadhaar seeded bank accounts through Direct \nBenefit Transfer (DBT).\nIn addition to this, the Central Government has taken the \n \nfollowing steps to cover more and more farmers under the PM\n-\nKISAN Scheme: \n-\n \n \n(i)\n \nState \nNodal Officers, District Nodal Officers and Block Nodal Officers had been \nappointed to monitor the scheme progress and provide necessary support to the farmers. \n \n \n(ii)\n \nStates/UTs have been asked to expedite the process of saturation of the Scheme \nby ensuring en\nrollment of all eligible farmer families.\n \n \n(iii)\n \nThe States /UTs have organized publicity/awareness camps to ensure expeditious \nverification of the data of the registered beneficiaries.\n \n \n\n(iv)\n \nGovernment of India conducts weekly meetings with the state nodal officers to \nreview the progress of the scheme  including  registration of the farmers. \n \n \n(v)\n \nThe Farmer Corner module has been provided on the portal. Through this module \nfarmers can self\n-\nregist\ner and check their status regarding eligibility, benefits transfer, etc.\n \n(vi)\n \nThe KYS module intended to provide the beneficiary status through a single \nwindow. It is a one\n-\nstop solution for the farmers.\n \n \n(vii)\n \nMore than 4 lakhs Common Service Centers across the coun\ntry have been \nonboarded to provide several facilities such as registration, details update, e\n-\nKYC etc. to \nthe farmers in assisted mode at their doorsteps. This has particularly helped the farmers \nwho had limitations to access the portal, mobile application\n, etc.\n \n \n(viii)\n \nThe PM Kisan mobile app was launched in February 2020 and the primary \nobjective of the app is to provide services of the PM\n-\nKISAN scheme on the fingertips of the \nfarmers. It is user\n-\nfriendly and easily downloadable from the Google Play Store.\n \n \n(ix)\n \nThe provision for e\n-\nKYC through face authentication feature was also provided \nthrough the PM\n-\nKISAN mobile app. This allows farmers, even in remote areas, to complete \ntheir e\n-\nKYC without the need for OTP or fingerprints, merely by scanning their faces. The \nprovision has been made to allow e\n-\nKYC of up to 100 other farmers in their neighborhood \nthrough the app. The Government Officials have also been allowed to complete 500 e\n-\nKYCs through their registered mobile numbers.\n \n \n*\n**\n \n \n \n\nAnnexure\n-\n1\n \nDetails of \nbenefi\nciaries\n \nunder PM\n-\nKISAN since its inception period\n-\nwise and state\n-\nwise.\n \nSr. \nNo.\n \nState/UT\n \nperiod\n \nPeriod\n \nPeriod\n \nPeriod\n \nPeriod\n \nPeriod\n \nPeriod\n \nPeriod\n \nPeriod\n \nPeriod\n \nPeriod\n \nPeriod\n \nPeriod\n \nPeriod\n \nDec\n-\nMarch\n \nApril\n-\nJuly\n \nAug\n-\nNov\n \nDec\n-\nMarch\n \nApril\n-\nJuly\n \nAug\n-\nNov\n \nDec\n-\nMarch\n \nApril\n-\nJuly\n \nAug\n-\nNov\n \nDec\n-\nMarch\n \nAp